<title>HUNGARY: Hungary 3-yr govt bond yield rises to 17.36 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary 3-yr govt bond yield rises to 17.36 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of Hungary's three-year government bonds was set by auction at 17.36 percent, up from 16.73 percent at an auction on March 13, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BONDS OF THE 2000/E SERIES</p>
<p>    First day of interest    18 April 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   12 May 2000</p>
<p>    Total on offer	    40,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received	3,110.26 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    3,110.26 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 3,700 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	  17.36 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		   98.37 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.00 percent, payable semi- anually starting from April 18, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
